{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## DECISION — DEFERRED per Option C (operator-approved 2026-08-29)\n\nOperator approved **Option C (defer)**. No code change this session — no classification added, no removal (the removal analysis is moot; see the reachability comment above, retained purely as CONTEXT for a future revisit — it strengthens the case that the raise is a legitimate dev/partial-install guard and should NOT be stripped).\n\n### Deferred plan (do NOT act on it now — only when the revisit trigger fires)\n**Deferred A-path:** IF `edit_workflow` is ever routed through `error_code_for` on a live surface (e.g. a future MCP edit tool, or any wiring that lets the bare `WorkflowError` at `editor.py:475` reach the classifier), THEN:\n- Add ONE new vocabulary code **`environment_unready`** to `KNOWN_ERROR_CODES` (+ `schemas/common.schema.json`, regenerated `docs/mcp-reference.md` via `gen_mcp_reference.py`, `tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json`). Semantics: *a required local build artifact / environment dependency is absent; the operation cannot run until the environment is built — NOT caller input, NOT an LLM/provider outage.*\n- Introduce a dedicated `WorkflowError` subclass (`WorkflowAssetsUnavailableError`) mirroring 35ab's `WorkflowUnknownStepError`; map it in `_workflow_caller_code`/`error_code_for`; raise it at `editor.py:475` (message preserved).\n- Keep the bare `WorkflowError` execute base → `llm_unavailable` (protects genuine execute-time outages; dbca AC3).\n- Held-out oracle asserting the CODE (not message), mutation-checked. Consumers to honor it = ONLY the new surface that exposes edit (today: zero).\n- Do NOT overload `not_found` (contractually \"caller named an unknown workflow/run\") or `invalid_input` (caller input is valid).\n\n### Revisit trigger\nThe missing-bundle path becoming **classifier-reachable on any live surface** — i.e. anything that makes `error_code_for` receive the `editor.py:475` exception (an MCP `edit_workflow` tool, a library facade that classifies it, etc.). Until then this stays parked; the CLI already prints the correct actionable message and no agent/structured surface observes a code.\n\n### Eventual-fix attribution (for whoever picks this up)\n- **caused_by:** `8a31-e1c3-cf31-4239` (biomedical-upper-tench, commit `77f1c4011c83`) — the blanket `LLMError`→`llm_unavailable` mapping; same origin dbca/35ab both cite.\n- **likely close class:** `plan_defect` (consistent with dbca and 35ab).\n\nParking to `idea` status (not-yet-actionable) so this reads as a deferred/backlog item, not active WIP.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788056061824503772,"uuid":"5dfc12c9-830b-469d-9d0e-1c17cc59b344"}